From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add riscv64-linux support

Wasmtime itself already publishes an official riscv64gc-linux C-API
release tarball (ziglang.org's build wouldn't matter here, but
bytecodealliance/wasmtime's own release process has shipped one since
well before this tag); wasmtime-py just never learned to ask for it.

plat_name_to_download_args() has no manylinux_2_39_riscv64 entry, so
`python -m build --wheel -C=--build-option=--plat-name
-C=--build-option=manylinux_2_39_riscv64` fails outright. Add one,
mapping to the ci/download-wasmtime.py arch "riscv64" - matching
`platform.machine()` on a riscv64 host, not Rust's "riscv64gc" triple
component - because wasmtime/_ffi.py's runtime loader looks up
`<sys_platform>-<platform.machine()>` to find the bundled shared
library directory.

download-wasmtime.py then needs its own translation the other way:
Wasmtime names the release asset
wasmtime-<version>-riscv64gc-linux-c-api.tar.xz, not
...-riscv64-linux-..., so the download step substitutes "riscv64gc"
into the asset filename while still extracting into the "linux-riscv64"
directory _ffi.py expects.

Finally, _ffi.py's own machine allow-list hard-fails on anything but
x86_64/aarch64; add riscv64 so the loader actually reaches the
directory the wheel now ships.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to bytecodealliance/wasmtime-py]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/ci/_custom_build/backend.py b/ci/_custom_build/backend.py
index 78dbb12..8a96ff8 100644
--- a/ci/_custom_build/backend.py
+++ b/ci/_custom_build/backend.py
@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@ def plat_name_to_download_args(plat_name:str) -> list[str]:
         'macosx-11-0-arm64':            ['darwin', 'arm64'],
         'manylinux1-x86_64':            ['linux', 'x86_64'],
         'manylinux2014_aarch64':        ['linux', 'aarch64'],
+        'manylinux_2_39_riscv64':       ['linux', 'riscv64'],
         'musllinux_1_2_x86_64':         ['musl', 'x86_64'],
         'musllinux_1_2_aarch64':        ['musl', 'aarch64'],
         'win-amd64':                    ['win32', 'x86_64'],
diff --git a/ci/download-wasmtime.py b/ci/download-wasmtime.py
index dc933d7..df03cf8 100644
--- a/ci/download-wasmtime.py
+++ b/ci/download-wasmtime.py
@@ -25,7 +25,12 @@ def main(platform, arch):
         arch = 'aarch64'
     dirname = '{}-{}'.format(platform, arch)
     if platform == 'linux' or platform == 'musl':
-        filename = 'wasmtime-{}-{}-{}-c-api.tar.xz'.format(version, arch, platform)
+        # Wasmtime's own release assets name the riscv64 Linux build after
+        # the Rust target triple's architecture component, "riscv64gc", not
+        # "riscv64" (what `uname -m`/`platform.machine()` report and what
+        # the wheel's directory name must match - see wasmtime/_ffi.py).
+        download_arch = 'riscv64gc' if arch == 'riscv64' else arch
+        filename = 'wasmtime-{}-{}-{}-c-api.tar.xz'.format(version, download_arch, platform)
         libname = '_libwasmtime.so'
         dirname = 'linux-{}'.format(arch)
     elif platform == 'win32':
diff --git a/wasmtime/_ffi.py b/wasmtime/_ffi.py
index c24a747..6763399 100644
--- a/wasmtime/_ffi.py
+++ b/wasmtime/_ffi.py
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ if machine == 'AMD64':
     machine = 'x86_64'
 if machine == 'arm64' or machine == 'ARM64':
     machine = 'aarch64'
-if machine != 'x86_64' and machine != 'aarch64':
+if machine != 'x86_64' and machine != 'aarch64' and machine != 'riscv64':
     raise RuntimeError("unsupported architecture for wasmtime: {}".format(machine))
 
 filename = Path(__file__).parent / (sys_platform + '-' + machine) / libname
-- 
2.43.0

